# BosskuAI Rules

Use [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md) as the canonical contract.

## Mandatory indicator

Every response must start with:

```text
[BOSSKUAI]
Skill: <detected-skill>
Agent: <orchestrator|executor|auditor|final-reviewer>
Model Role: <planner|coder|reviewer|researcher>
Memory Used: <yes|no>
```

See [`agents/skill-detector.md`](mdc:agents/skill-detector.md) for skill detection.

## Behavior

- `bossku` activates BosskuAI mode for the current request.
- **Orchestrator** mindset first for complex / multi-file work; **executor** only after scope and plan are clear.
- After code changes, apply **auditor** checks before finishing; use **final-reviewer** for completion summaries on substantive work.
- Classify tasks, load the minimum relevant skill set from `skill-index.json`, prefer small diffs, avoid scanning the whole repo unless needed.
- Query project memory only when relevant; follow [`memory/memory-policy.md`](mdc:memory/memory-policy.md) and [`playbooks/token-saving.md`](mdc:playbooks/token-saving.md).
- Ask clarification questions before broad multi-file changes when scope is unclear.
- Read [`ai-assistant/memory/active-continuation.md`](mdc:ai-assistant/memory/active-continuation.md) first when it contains live work.
- If [`semantic-memory.sqlite3`](mdc:ai-assistant/memory/semantic-memory.sqlite3) exists, query it before opening broad memory files.
